    "openapi_lint_cause": "Redocly lint: 3 errors, `Property nullable is not expected here` (struct rule) at IvrAuditEvidenceRow.reason/before_state_json/after_state_json. nullable is an OpenAPI 3.0 keyword; the spec is openapi: 3.1.0. Introduced by W-0307 (6029b19, 2026-09-16, draft.29). Reproduced on this machine in node:24-bookworm-slim on `git archive HEAD` of 1091496: `npm --prefix deploy/ci run openapi:lint` exits 1.",
    "why_local_was_green": "deploy/ci/gate-invocations.json had no Redocly gate; the local sweep ran validate-openapi.mjs, openapi-contract-drift.mjs and selftest-openapi.mjs, none of which lints struct.",
    "consequence": "validate fails, so no build/test/security/privacy/publish/deploy job has run on the hosted pipeline since at least 2026-09-21.",
    "fix": "W-0354: contract 1.0.0-draft.33 writes the three fields as type: [string, 'null']; deploy/ci/scripts/openapi-lint-gate.mjs joins the local sweep with two negative controls."
  },
